        "original_id": "a0fd97f8-cc8d-5805-bac2-349e235cde9f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Chicago Rockford International Airport, Rockford, Chicago, McClellan–Palomar Airport, Carlsbad, San Diego County, California, Fort Collins–Loveland Municipal Airport\n- Companies: Elite Airways\n- Topics: Airport locations, airport routes, airport identifiers\n\nFacts:\n- Chicago Rockford International Airport is located four miles (6 km) south of downtown Rockford and 85 miles northwest of Chicago.\n- McClellan–Palomar Airport, also called Palomar Airport, is a public airport three miles (5 km) southeast of Carlsbad in San Diego County, California.\n- McClellan–Palomar Airport has the identifiers IATA CLD, ICAO KCRQ, and FAA LID CRQ.\n- Fort Collins–Loveland Municipal Airport supports commercial nonstop flights to Chicago Rockford International Airport operated by Elite Airways.",
